{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["The letter heh in <b>החמשים</b> (\"the fifty\") draws itself and another with it. Some say that Korah was among those swallowed, and the earth swallowed \"them and Korah.\" Some say he was among the burned, and the witness is \"and Korah, when the assembly died,\" in the fire's consuming. And our Sages said that he was both burned and swallowed. In my opinion, only the place of Dathan and Abiram split open, for it is not mentioned. Rather, Korah was standing with his fire-pan, with Aaron and with the princes of the assembly who were offering incense. And the meaning of the verse \"and Korah\" is not joined to \"and it swallowed them,\" but rather to \"when the assembly died.\" And if someone objects and asks why Korah was not mentioned among the burned, the answer is that since Scripture mentioned that his assembly that came to aid him was burned, there is no need to mention Korah, for by a fortiori inference the matter is known. Similarly, \"Pharaoh's chariots and his army\" — in the Song [of the Sea] Pharaoh himself is not mentioned as drowning, yet truly he drowned, for thus it is written: \"Pharaoh and his army were tossed\" [n]. And the trustworthy witness is that Korah was among the burned, \"and let him not be like Korah and his assembly.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's reference ונער פרעה וחילו (literally 'Pharaoh's boy/lad and his army') appears to be his paraphrastic citation of Exodus 15:4, where the verse reads ונאר פרעה וחילו ('Pharaoh's army'). The word ונער is textually uncertain; I translate it hyper-literally as 'tossed' reading it as related to נער ('to shake/toss'), though the biblical verse has נאר (= נאצר, 'chosen/picked'). The final quote is from Numbers 17:5 (English 16:40)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:11.019561548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}